  "_comment": [
    "One config entry, and it exists only so the two seeded devices survive Home Assistant's load.",
    "",
    "Since HA 2026.8 a device belongs to exactly one config entry (core PR #175785, 'Restrict",
    "device registry entries to single config entry and subentry'). The device registry storage",
    "went from 1.12 to 3.x, and the migration from 1.x silently DROPS every device whose",
    "config_entries is empty (helpers/device_registry.py, DeviceRegistryStore._async_migrate_func:",
    "'Drop devices that have no config entry / subentry pairs'). The seeded devices had none, so",
    "on 2026.8+ they were gone before anything could ask for them — issue #156. An entity anchor",
    "no longer helps, and once loaded, async_cleanup strips a config_entry_id that is not in this",
    "file, which in the single-entry model removes the device as well.",
    "",
    "So the entry has to exist here, and it must be one HA keeps without setting anything up.",
    "`acme` is an integration that is not installed: the shape a real house has after a custom",
    "integration is removed from custom_components while its entry, devices and entities stay",
    "behind. Probed on 2026.10.4: the entry loads as `not_loaded`, nothing is set up, nothing",
    "is logged, no repair is raised, and both devices survive the migration and the cleanup.",
    "A DISABLED entry for a real integration (e.g. `demo`) also keeps the devices, but is not a",
    "shape HA produces — disabling an entry cascades disabled_by onto its devices and entities —",
    "and an enabled `demo` entry would set up demo's own fleet of entities and devices.",
    "",
    "Synthetic, written by hand: the reference instance's core.config_entries is never captured",
    "(SPEC-realdata-fixture.md §5). Key set and minor_version taken from the loader in the image",
    "(config_entries.py, ConfigEntries.async_initialize), which indexes these keys directly."
  ],
